course: dictionary
lesson: 14066
title: Mathematical: more than maths
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Mathematical» is an adjective, so it describes a noun. Its first meaning is to do with maths. «We solved a mathematical problem about shapes.» The clue is the word problem with shapes: this is a problem that uses numbers, shapes or calculations.
explain: The word also means done carefully, exactly and logically, like a calculation. «Sara worked out the answer in a neat, mathematical way, one step at a time.» Here the clues are neat and one step at a time: nothing was guessed, and each step followed from the last.
explain: Look at how the word is used in phrases. «There is mathematical certainty that 5 + 5 makes 10.» Certainty means being sure, and mathematical certainty means exact and as sure as numbers can show. A «mathematical mind» means someone who thinks logically, so you can ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Mathematical» means to do with mathematics.
fact: «Mathematical» is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as a problem or a symbol.
fact: Mathematical symbols include +, −, × and ÷, and the sign =.
fact: «Mathematical certainty» means exact, as sure as numbers can show.
fact: Someone with a «mathematical mind» thinks logically, step by step.
exercise: «The class solved a mathematical problem about shapes.» What does mathematical mean here? | To do with painting | Written in a diary | Very loud | *To do with maths
exercise: «Sara worked out the answer in a neat, mathematical way, one step at a time.» What does mathematical suggest here? | Fast and messy | *Exact and logical, step by step | Loud and silly | Guessed without thinking
exercise: «Ben drew the plus sign, a mathematical symbol.» What is a mathematical symbol? | *A sign such as +, −, × or ÷ | A picture of a cat | A word that rhymes with maths | A small bag for pencils
test: «There is mathematical certainty that 5 + 5 makes 10.» What does mathematical certainty mean? | *Exact, as sure as numbers can show | Maybe, but probably not | Very quiet, like a whisper | A guess made in the dark
test: «Her mathematical mind spotted the pattern at once.» What does a mathematical mind mean? | Someone who likes painting | Someone who is always late | *Someone who thinks logically | A mind full of loud noise
exam: Jayden says «mathematical» only ever means something in a maths lesson. Is he right? | No, it means very loud | *No, it also means careful, exact and logical | Yes, it only ever means something in a maths lesson | Yes, and it only means numbers
